# The repositories whose queued jobs this Mac answers, one `owner/name` per line.
#
# Empty, which is what switched off means: `tart-runner` polls nothing, and its
# LaunchAgent is not loaded either. It is the fallback for a *private* repository
# that has run out of GitHub's free macOS minutes — never a public one, where
# anyone who can open a pull request could then run code on this Mac.
#
# A repository added here also needs `runs-on: [self-hosted, macOS, tart]` in its
# workflow, an image to clone (`tart-runner --build-image`), and the agent loaded.
# The repository README has the whole procedure.
#
# A file rather than a constant in the script, so that adding one is a line here
# and nothing else — the LaunchAgent would otherwise carry the list in its plist,
# where a change means a bootout and a fresh bootstrap.
